  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education vocational training - WE4D Employment Promotion for Women for Green Transformation in Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of WE4D is to improve the employment and economic situation of women in Africa, especially in companies and sectors that promote the green transformation of the economy. The programme is implemented in the following fields of action: (1) labour market-oriented education and training, (2) transition to the labour market, (3) employment in value chains, (4) competitiveness of start-ups and MSMEs and (5) regional scaling of approaches. To promote the green transformation, WE4D focuses on green sectors (Sustainable Agriculture/ Agroprocessing, Circular Economy/ Waste Management/ Biomass, Eco-Tourism, Blue Economy and Aquaculture, Renewable Energy) and conventional sectors with a potential for greening (Construction, Transport and Logistics). Persons with disabilities (PwD) are among the target groups of the project. The programme will be implemented in six countries: Kenya, Malawi, Mozambique, South Africa, Tanzania, and Uganda.</narrative>
  </description>
